class.description:
The [GCASPacker] is used to create GCAS packages that can be loaded into a running project using [method ProjectSettings.load_resource_pack], like PCK packages created with [PCKPacker].
GCAS packages are content-addressed: files are split into chunks, identical chunks are only stored once, and each chunk is compressed independently, so files can still be read from any position (e.g. when streaming textures). A package can be a patch for other GCAS packages (see [method add_base_pack]), in which case it only contains the chunks that aren't in them.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var packer = GCASPacker.new()
packer.start("user://dlc.gcas")
packer.add_file("res://text.txt", "text.txt")
packer.flush()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var packer = new GCASPacker();
packer.Start("user://dlc.gcas");
packer.AddFile("res://text.txt", "text.txt");
packer.Flush();
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
